Open sets of a domain as maps into the Sierpiński system.

<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`sierpinski`).** The Sierpiński neighbourhood system on a singleton has the empty set and the singleton as neighbourhoods, with master the singleton.

*Proof.* The filter axioms hold for these two sets. ∎

**Definition (`mapOfOpen`).** An open set of ideal elements determines an approximable map into Sierpiński by relating a domain neighbourhood to the singleton precisely when the corresponding basic open lies in the open set, and relating freely to the empty neighbourhood.

*Proof.* Domain and codomain membership, master, intersection on the right, and monotonicity unpack the open-set axioms. ∎

**Theorem (`mapOfOpen_rel_empty`).** Relating to the empty Sierpiński neighbourhood is domain membership together with membership of some principal in the open set.

*Proof.* Unpack the defining cases. ∎

**Definition (`openOfMap`).** The open set of a map into Sierpiński consists of those ideal elements for which some principal neighbourhood relates to the singleton.

*Proof.* By definition. ∎

**Theorem (`openOfMap_isOpen`).** The open set of a map into Sierpiński is open.

*Proof.* Witness basic opens via relating neighbourhoods. ∎

**Definition (`openIso`).** Open subsets are order-isomorphic to approximable maps into Sierpiński.

*Proof.* The round trips are the previous constructions; order equivalence compares membership via principals. ∎

**Definition (`opensReprIso`).** Open subsets are order-isomorphic to ideal elements of the function space into Sierpiński.

*Proof.* Compose the previous isomorphism with the function-space element isomorphism. ∎
